      "fund": "Substack / C-Suites",
      "date": "February 15, 2026",
      "summary": "Argues that Yelp's low valuation multiple is a market misclassification of its economic balance sheet, noting its structural lease liabilities are mistaken for debt while it generates $1.41B in revenue and $133M in net income with a clean EBIT profile. Estimates an intrinsic value of $40 per share (~90% upside) driven by durable cash flows, strong paying-location density across 496,000 merchants, and relentless share buybacks.",
