      "fund": "r/ValueInvesting",
      "date": "October 15, 2025",
      "summary": "Outlines a bullish value thesis centered on Yelp's successful transition into a lead-generation marketplace for high-ticket home and local Services, which accounts for ~64% of revenue with significantly higher ARPU ($926/quarter per location vs. $443 for restaurants). Points to key operational catalysts including corporate restructuring, non-Bay Area headcount optimization, reduced stock-based compensation, and steady EPS expansion.",
